{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01LQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:570a1eea99bb1bbb2b32618121cd7b956b9c3ea97598f22c219f5f3330122199", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma says among other things that forming the\nrelative spectrum commutes with base change.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b00657d857ab1e3264d553143af0b721adbd22a50831c91e2b9b03565d78e6ed", "unit_id": "tag:01LQ:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01LQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi : \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\to S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\pi^{-1}(U)$", "MATH_0009": "$g : S' \\to S$", "MATH_0010": "$S' \\times_S \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A}) =\n\\underline{\\Spec}_{S'}(g^*\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\mathcal{A}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A})}\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-spec-properties}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:440f9c17e761b78d1e93a494d5436fcfd55346936f38c19b0c9334687b8baec8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2463bbce01334e9f753c2ac05f611193fb03f1c3811fd2095765aa1b947d4243", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\nsheaf of <MATH_0003>-algebras. Let\n<MATH_0004>\nbe the relative spectrum of <MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> For every affine open <MATH_0007> the inverse image\n<MATH_0008> is affine.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every morphism <MATH_0009> we have\n<MATH_0010>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThe universal map\n<MATH_0011>\nis an isomorphism of <MATH_0012>-algebras.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a3e22c7ab165b8d421017ead7ec34ddce75d9022186d1a0588ccb6ffc6df823", "unit_id": "tag:01LX:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01LQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-relative-spec}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-spec-base-change}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-spec-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3373d69d1a771d1b240d3f94798edce7e161caf54de4b2de49dd8524c8dc1502", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a427614da802d886ca4a19824be569f890c6aae0d5a2fcfabb5260d7b8e4f3ca", "source_text": "Part (1) comes from the description of the relative spectrum\nby glueing, see Lemma <REF_0001>.\nPart (2) follows immediately from Lemma <REF_0002>.\nPart (3) follows because it is local on <MATH_0001> and it is clear in case <MATH_0002>\nis affine by Lemma <REF_0003> for example.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:371bc1390823f8ad89dd105a676807d8e4562190664dd68730bcc912933514d9", "unit_id": "tag:01LX:proof"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01LQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$$\ncan : X \\longrightarrow \\underline{\\Spec}_S(f_*\\mathcal{O}_X)\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0007": "$can|_{f^{-1}(U)}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\nf^{-1}(U) \\longrightarrow \\Spec(\\Gamma(f^{-1}(U), \\mathcal{O}_X))\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-push-forward-quasi-coherent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-morphism-into-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-canonical-morphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e3a397016183006d8fded3a174ee56bddb1e1af090cc8b7ca5621253b45a59fd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ae03f7d68dc1e4c481560db211b235dac315eeb175b242a9c22760e2a01f08e9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism\nof schemes. By Schemes, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe sheaf <MATH_0002> is a quasi-coherent sheaf of\n<MATH_0003>-algebras. There is a canonical morphism\n<MATH_0004>\nof schemes over <MATH_0005>.\nFor any affine open <MATH_0006> the restriction <MATH_0007>\nis identified with the canonical morphism\n<MATH_0008>\ncoming from Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70c0b01e4aca29e8d4cf63bde8ecd699c52d21ee6029a1ef207ea45a25288a8d", "unit_id": "tag:01LY:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01LQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\underline{\\Spec}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi : f^*f_*\\mathcal{O}_X \\to \\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\text{id} : f_*\\mathcal{O}_X \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-spec-affine}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:35f5facfa39c0b441be723241d5f36774a506bf74a407d401e02c7fc5c8ebc7a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f6bf6c6e9dcdf3c317917b01a7bd53df25ca1281cd463ba3af0601814294ce67", "source_text": "The morphism comes, via the definition of <MATH_0001>\nas the scheme representing the functor <MATH_0002>, from the canonical map\n<MATH_0003> (which by adjointness of\npush and pull corresponds to\n<MATH_0004>).\nThe statement on the restriction to <MATH_0005>\nfollows from the description of the relative spectrum over\naffines, see Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5a46bb2b721ed97bd9a6f43baf51ce97c896b43000354f9ae7b515dbccae3949", "unit_id": "tag:01LY:proof"}
